---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ConsultForm from '../components/ConsultForm.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="CFO Market Intelligence | Lozen Advisory" description="Independent CFO-focused intelligence on AI ROI, agentic AI controls, accountability, workforce exposure, insurance signals, and the financial implications of emerging governance risk.">
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="grid-bg"></div>
  <div class="wrap inner">
    <div class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="/#services">Services</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; CFO Market Intelligence</div>
    <span class="pill">Independent CFO Intelligence</span>
    <div class="ic-lg"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:52px;height:52px;color:var(--accent-2)"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/></svg></div>
    <h1>CFO Market Intelligence</h1>
    <p class="sub">AI deployment is accelerating. Finance is still being asked to prove the return, explain the controls, and identify who owns the risk.</p>
    <div class="hero-cta">
      <a href="#consult" class="btn btn-accent">Request CFO Intelligence →</a>
      <a href="#how" class="btn btn-ghost">How it works</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div class="prose reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Overview</span>
      <h2 class="h2">The CFO problem is not a lack of AI information. It is a lack of decision-grade intelligence.</h2>
      <p>CFOs are under pressure to demonstrate AI ROI while deployment speed is moving ahead of updated controls, internal expertise, explainability, and clear accountability.</p>
      <p>Lozen Advisory separates material financial and governance signals from vendor claims and market noise, then translates them into the questions finance leadership must be able to answer before an auditor, regulator, insurer, board, or incident forces the issue.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="checklist" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>AI ROI and value-realization analysis</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Agentic AI control and accountability signals</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>D&amp;O, insurance, and disclosure implications</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Auditability and operating-record gaps</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Verification labor and finance-capacity exposure</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>CFO and board decision implications</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What the intelligence resolves</span>
      <h2 class="h2">From market signal to finance decision</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/></svg></div><h3>ROI scrutiny</h3><p>Distinguish measurable enterprise value from adoption volume, speed claims, and uncounted human verification work.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="18" y1="20" x2="18" y2="10"/><line x1="12" y1="20" x2="12" y2="4"/><line x1="6" y1="20" x2="6" y2="14"/></svg></div><h3>Control exposure</h3><p>Identify where agentic AI is taking or recommending actions faster than internal controls are being updated.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/></svg></div><h3>Auditability</h3><p>Test whether finance can explain what an AI agent did, what it relied on, and who authorized the result.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg></div><h3>Accountability ownership</h3><p>Locate where responsibility for a material AI error is named, diffused, or left with no one.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg></div><h3>Finance capacity</h3><p>Expose the internal expertise, review time, and exception-handling burden required to make AI outputs usable.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"/></svg></div><h3>Independent intelligence</h3><p>Provide a concise CFO briefing that is not tied to a software sale, implementation mandate, or vendor adoption agenda.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h2 class="h2">A clear advisory process</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">1</div><h3>Frame</h3><p>Define the ROI, control, accountability, or financial-risk question the CFO needs answered.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">2</div><h3>Investigate</h3><p>Examine current market evidence, regulation, insurance signals, operating assumptions, and enterprise exposure.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">3</div><h3>Translate</h3><p>Convert fragmented AI developments into financial, control, disclosure, workforce, and governance implications.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">4</div><h3>Brief</h3><p>Deliver a focused CFO intelligence product with decision questions, exposure signals, and an executive discussion.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Common questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>How is this different from vendor research?</h4><p>Lozen Advisory does not sell AI software or measure success by deployment. The analysis begins with the CFO decision, tests the underlying evidence, and identifies the financial and governance exposure that adoption reporting may omit.</p></div>
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>What CFO questions can the work address?</h4><p>Typical questions involve AI ROI, agentic controls, auditability, unclear accountability, insurance exposure, verification labor, legislation, disclosure, or whether reported productivity gains are financially complete.</p></div>
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>What does the CFO receive?</h4><p>A concise independent analysis of the material signal, the enterprise exposure, what current reporting may be missing, and the questions finance and the board should resolve next.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<ConsultForm serviceHighlight="cfo market intelligence" selectedService="CFO Market Intelligence" />
</BaseLayout>
